# Line endings.  This checkout is on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so
# without rules here every new file is converted to CRLF on checkout.  Anything
# that ships to a Linux host has to stay LF: a CRLF shebang is
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a CRLF after a line-continuation backslash
# silently changes the command.  The web pages and the PHP proxy are served
# verbatim, so their bytes must not drift either.
#
# Per-project rules stay with their project (dashboard/.gitattributes,
# tsguard/.gitattributes); this only covers what lives at the workspace root and
# in the folders that have no rules of their own (ops/, tmd-radar/).

.gitattributes text eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.php   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Windows-side tooling.  CRLF is correct here and harmless.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
